{"uncertainty": 0.15, "outcome": "I wrote the RTL for a four-requester round-robin arbiter (rr_arbiter.v), a self-checking testbench that runs N=4 and N=5 side by side (rr_arbiter_tb.v), and one SymbiYosys proof file (rr_arbiter.sby). They follow the approved interface and microarchitecture specs. The tool runs I made while working were advisory only and are not evidence. The platform's own checks and an independent review still have to be done.", "artifacts": [{"kind": "design_note", "title": "Implementation decisions against the microarchitecture", "summary": "Built as [artifact:prj-1c32d8ed92.microarchitecture.a1] describes, for [requirement:req-142be1ce31]. The only state is a $clog2(N)-bit pointer, reset synchronously to 0 when rst_n is low. The grant comes from a combinational search that starts at the pointer and wraps by comparing with LAST (N-1), not by counter overflow, so N values that are not powers of two work. The pointer moves to one past the winner only on a cycle with a grant, and holds when nothing is requested. Every output of the combinational block gets a default first, so no latch is inferred. The formal properties sit under `ifdef FORMAL` and are the ones [artifact:prj-1c32d8ed92.interface-spec.a1] section 6 asks for. Departures from the verification plan: (1) there is only one .sby file, at N=4, because the platform accepts exactly one formal_spec, so the planned rr_arbiter_n5.sby is not included and N=5 is checked only in simulation; (2) the planned rr_arbiter_tb_fail.v failure-path testbench is not included."}], "files": [{"path": "rr_arbiter.v", "kind": "rtl_source", "title": "rr_arbiter RTL", "summary": "Parameterised round-robin arbiter (N=4 by default) with the ports in [artifact:prj-1c32d8ed92.interface-spec.a1]: clk, rst_n (active low, synchronous), req[N-1:0] and grant[N-1:0]. It is built as [artifact:prj-1c32d8ed92.microarchitecture.a1] describes and serves [requirement:req-142be1ce31]. The formal properties under `ifdef FORMAL` are: the pointer stays in range and is 0 after reset; the grant is one-hot or zero, goes only to a requester, and someone is granted whenever anyone asks; no asking requester lies between the pointer and the winner; after a grant the pointer is one past the winner, and it holds when nothing is requested; and each requester's wait is at most N-1, with an induction invariant that the wait plus the pointer's distance to the requester stays within N-1. Covers: each requester granted, all requesting at once, the pointer wrapping from N-1 to 0, and each requester waiting N-1 cycles.", "entry": "rr_arbiter"}, {"path": "rr_arbiter_tb.v", "kind": "testbench", "title": "rr_arbiter self-checking testbench (N=4 and N=5)", "summary": "Runs N=4 and N=5 arbiters side by side, as planned in [artifact:prj-1c32d8ed92.microarchitecture.a1]. Each cycle it checks grant against a reference pointer model, and it checks the strict 0..N-1 rotation after reset with everyone requesting. Per-requester wait counters fail the run with $error if any wait exceeds N-1. Coverage goals fail the run if not reached: no requests, each requester alone, everyone requesting, a held request while the others change, a wait of exactly N-1, and reset during traffic, as listed in [artifact:prj-1c32d8ed92.interface-spec.a1] section 6. It reads the nonce with $value$plusargs and prints the NIRMAAN-SIM verdict once, just before $finish.", "entry": "rr_arbiter_tb"}, {"path": "rr_arbiter.sby", "kind": "formal_spec", "title": "rr_arbiter unbounded proof setup, N=4", "summary": "One SymbiYosys job with no [tasks] section: mode prove, depth 20 (the induction depth), smtbmc engine, reading rr_arbiter.v with read -formal and prep -top rr_arbiter. It proves the properties [artifact:prj-1c32d8ed92.interface-spec.a1] section 6 requires, at the default N of 4.", "entry": "rr_arbiter"}], "tool_runs": [], "claims": ["While working I ran lint, simulation (Icarus), formal prove and formal cover on these files through the broker, and each reported a pass. Those runs were advisory and cannot be cited as evidence.", "The proof covers only N=4. N=5 (not a power of two) is checked only by the testbench.", "I did not run synthesis myself. That the design synthesizes with no latches is expected from the coding style, not shown."], "escalation": null, "notes": "Still to do before signoff: the platform's lint, simulation, synthesis, formal and cover runs, and an independent review. Two departures from the verification plan for the tech lead to accept or reject: the planned N=5 proof file (rr_arbiter_n5.sby) is left out because the platform takes only one formal_spec file, and the planned failure-path testbench (rr_arbiter_tb_fail.v) is not delivered."}

